# Design System Rules

- Use existing design tokens and shared component primitives before adding new styling patterns.
- Avoid hardcoded visual literals (hex colors, spacing, radius, shadows) when an existing token already covers the need.
- Prefer composition and consistency over custom one-off components.
- Include explicit UI states for async surfaces: `loading`, `empty`, `error`, `ready`.
- Keep interactions accessible (keyboard support, focus visibility, semantic labels).
- Use plain-language error messages with actionable recovery guidance.
- Keep visual hierarchy clear: primary actions obvious, destructive actions confirmed.
